---

# 1. Problem Statement

Customers may enter the loan application flow through an offer-based entry point. The offer contains customer and loan information that should be used to streamline application completion.

The offer itself is an internal artifact and must not be displayed to the customer. The system should leverage the offer data to prepopulate application fields, persist the information, and submit it as part of the pricing workflow.

---

# 2. Goals

### Primary Goals

* Reduce customer data entry.
* Improve application completion rates.
* Ensure consistent pricing inputs.
* Persist offer-derived information with the application.

### Non-Goals

* Displaying offer details to customers.
* Allowing customers to view offer metadata.
* Supporting manual offer selection within the UI.

---

# 3. User Experience

### Customer Journey

1. Customer launches application using an offer-based entry point.
2. System retrieves associated offer data.
3. Application fields are prefilled.
4. Customer reviews and updates editable information.
5. Customer submits application.
6. System persists application data.
7. System submits pricing request.

---

# 4. Offer Data Model

The offer may contain:

| Field               | Description                 |
| ------------------- | --------------------------- |
| Offer ID            | Internal offer identifier   |
| Customer First Name | Prefill value               |
| Customer Last Name  | Prefill value               |
| Address             | Prefill value               |
| City                | Prefill value               |
| State               | Prefill value               |
| Zip Code            | Prefill value               |
| Loan Amount         | Requested loan amount       |
| Loan Term           | Requested loan term         |
| Customer Identifier | Internal customer reference |

---

# 5. Functional Requirements

## FR-1 Offer Retrieval

The system shall retrieve the offer using the offer identifier supplied through the application entry point.

### Acceptance Criteria

* Offer retrieval occurs before rendering application data.
* Invalid offers are rejected.
* Expired offers are rejected.

---

## FR-2 Application Prefill

The system shall use offer data to prepopulate application fields.

### Prefilled Fields

| Field          | Source |
| -------------- | ------ |
| First Name     | Offer  |
| Last Name      | Offer  |
| Address Line 1 | Offer  |
| Address Line 2 | Offer  |
| City           | Offer  |
| State          | Offer  |
| Zip Code       | Offer  |
| Loan Amount    | Offer  |
| Loan Term      | Offer  |

### Acceptance Criteria

* Fields are populated automatically.
* Missing values remain editable.
* Customer-entered values override prefilled values.

---

## FR-3 Offer Visibility

The system shall not display offer information to the customer.

### Acceptance Criteria

The UI shall not display:

* Offer ID
* Offer Status
* Offer Expiration
* Offer Metadata
* Internal Pricing Attributes

---

## FR-4 Application Persistence

The system shall persist offer-derived values as part of the application record.

### Persisted Attributes

* Application ID
* Customer Information
* Loan Amount
* Loan Term
* Offer Reference ID
* Application Status

---

## FR-5 Pricing Submission

The system shall submit offer-derived loan information to Pricing.

### Pricing Inputs

| Attribute      | Source            |
| -------------- | ----------------- |
| Application ID | Application       |
| Customer ID    | Offer/Application |
| Loan Amount    | Offer/Application |
| Loan Term      | Offer/Application |

---

# 6. User Interface Requirements

## Application Start Page

### Purpose

Initialize application and retrieve offer data.

### Displayed Components

* Application Header
* Welcome Message
* Continue Button

### Hidden Components

* Offer Identifier
* Offer Context

---

## Personal Information Page

### Purpose

Collect and validate customer information.

### Fields

| Field         | Prefilled |
| ------------- | --------- |
| First Name    | Yes       |
| Last Name     | Yes       |
| Address       | Yes       |
| Phone Number  | No        |
| Email Address | No        |

### Rules

* Editable fields may be modified.
* Changes are persisted.

---

## Loan Information Page

### Purpose

Display loan request details.

### Fields

| Field       | Prefilled |
| ----------- | --------- |
| Loan Amount | Yes       |
| Loan Term   | Yes       |

### Rules

* Editable or read-only behavior determined by product configuration.

---

## Review and Submit Page

### Purpose

Allow customer review before submission.

### Displayed Sections

* Personal Information
* Loan Information
* Terms and Disclosures
* Submit Action

---

# 7. API Contract Expectations

## Retrieve Offer

GET /offers/{offerId}

### Response

```json
{
  "offerId": "OFF123",
  "customer": {
    "firstName": "John",
    "lastName": "Smith",
    "address": {
      "line1": "123 Main St",
      "city": "Phoenix",
      "state": "AZ",
      "zip": "85001"
    }
  },
  "loan": {
    "amount": 25000,
    "term": 60
  }
}
```

---

## Create Application

POST /applications

### Request

```json
{
  "offerId": "OFF123",
  "customer": {},
  "loan": {}
}
```

---

## Submit Pricing Request

POST /pricing/evaluate

### Request

```json
{
  "applicationId": "APP12345",
  "customerId": "C12345",
  "loanAmount": 25000,
  "loanTerm": 60
}
```

---

# 8. Error Handling

| Scenario           | Behavior                                |
| ------------------ | --------------------------------------- |
| Offer Not Found    | Display application unavailable message |
| Offer Expired      | Prevent application initiation          |
| Missing Offer Data | Continue with editable fields           |
| Pricing Failure    | Display retry or support message        |

---

# 9. Security Requirements

### SR-1

Offer identifiers shall not be displayed in the UI.

### SR-2

Offer data shall be encrypted in transit.

### SR-3

Offer data shall be encrypted at rest.

### SR-4

Only authorized backend services may access offer details.

### SR-5

Internal pricing attributes shall never be exposed to customers.

---

# 10. Audit Requirements

The system shall capture:

* Offer retrieval timestamp
* Offer identifier
* Application identifier
* Customer modifications
* Pricing submission timestamp
* Submission outcome

---

# 11. Success Metrics

* Reduced customer data entry effort.
* Increased application completion rate.
* Reduced pricing input errors.
* Successful offer-to-pricing traceability.

---

# 12. Key Principle

The offer is an internal business artifact. Customers interact with a standard loan application experience while the platform uses offer data behind the scenes to prefill application information, persist application state, and support downstream pricing processes.
